BEGIN_PGML We will define the probability of an event as the number of ways the event can happen divided by the total number of things that can happen.
END_PGML
############################################################ # Scaffold ############################################################ Scaffold::Begin(numbered => 1,is_open => "correct_or_first_incorrect",can_open => when_previous_correct,);
############################################################ # Section ############################################################ Section::Begin("");
BEGIN_PGML Suppose you roll two dice (one red and one green). How many total outcomes are there?
[_]{Compute(6*6)}{5}
END_PGML
Section::End();
############################################################ # Section ############################################################ Section::Begin("");
BEGIN_PGML Of those outcomes, how many have _different_ numbers on the two dice?
[_]{Compute(6*5)}{5}
END_PGML
############################################################ # Hint ############################################################ #Set value of $showHint in PGcourse.pl for course-wide attempt threshhold for revealing hints
BEGIN_PGML_HINT How many sequences of two different numbers can you make using the numbers 1 to 6?
END_PGML_HINT
Section::End();
############################################################ # Section ############################################################ Section::Begin("");
BEGIN_PGML Combining the two numbers your found above, what is the probability that two dice will show different numbers?
[_]{Compute(30/36)}{5}
END_PGML
Section::End();
############################################################ # Section ############################################################ Section::Begin("");
BEGIN_PGML What is the probability that you will get three different numbers when rolling three dice? (Assume the dice are different colors).
[_]{Compute((6*5*4)/(6**3))}{5}
END_PGML
Section::End();
